Scope 3

[AR 43c] The Group’s GHG emissions reporting includes biogenic CO 2 emissions resulting from the combustion or biodegradation of biomass, as well as emissions of other types of GHGs, notably CH 4 and N 2 O.

[AR 46] For the assessment of Scope 3 GHG emissions, the Group:

[AR 43d] The Group’s reported GHG emissions do not include purchased, sold or transferred removals or carbon credits, or GHG allowances.

• draws on the principles, requirements and guidelines of the GHG Protocol Corporate Value Chain (Scope 3) (Version 2011) and breaks down its total Scope 3 emissions into the 15 categories de ˱ned by the GHG Protocol;

[AR 43e] For activities falling within the scope of EU-ETS regulations, emissions reported under Scope 1 follow the same methodology.

• performs an annual reassessment of Scope 3 emissions for each reported category;

[AR 44] In calculating the percentage of Scope 1 GHG emissions covered by the EU ETS regulations presented above, the Group:

• identi ˱es and discloses the signi˱cant Scope 3 categories in relation to the Group’s total GHG emissions and according to the criteria de˱ned by the GHG Protocol;

• takes into account the GHG emissions of the installations it operates and which are subject to the EU-ETS regulations;

• includes emissions of CO 2 , CH 4 , N 2 0 and ˳uorinated gases;

• follows the same annual reporting periods for Scope 1 GHG emissions and emissions covered by the EU ETS;

• excludes from the carbon footprint reporting presented for the Group the following Scope 3 GHG emissions categories as they are not signi ˱cant compared with the total GHG emissions reported by the Group or because they are not relevant given the Group’s scope of activities:

• Scope 3.4 “Upstream Transportation and Distribution”,

• Scope 3.5 “Waste Generated in Operations”,

• Scope 3.8 “Upstream Leased Assets”,

• calculates the percentage using the following formula: (GHG emissions (in t CO 2 eq.) from installations subject to the EU-ETS regulations + national ETS + non-EU ETS)/(total Scope 1 GHG emissions in t CO 2 eq.).

